$ memtest
==== Q2: memtest ====
[1. start]
   total_pages=57066 free_pages=56790 user_pages=3 resident=3
   pt_pages=66 (user_pt=1 kernel_pt=64, +1 page directory)
[2a. after sbrk(64 pages) + touching them]
   total_pages=57066 free_pages=56726 user_pages=67 resident=67
   pt_pages=66 (user_pt=1 kernel_pt=64, +1 page directory)
   -> free pages dropped by 64 (64 data pages; the existing page table already covers them)
[2b. after malloc(40 pages) + touching them]
   total_pages=57066 free_pages=56685 user_pages=108 resident=108
   pt_pages=66 (user_pt=1 kernel_pt=64, +1 page directory)
   -> free pages dropped by 41
[3. just before fork()]
   total_pages=57066 free_pages=56685 user_pages=108 resident=108
   pt_pages=66 (user_pt=1 kernel_pt=64, +1 page directory)
[3. parent, child still alive]
   total_pages=57066 free_pages=56510 user_pages=108 resident=108
   pt_pages=66 (user_pt=1 kernel_pt=64, +1 page directory)
   -> fork() consumed 175 pages (copy of user pages + page tables + pgdir + kernel stack)
[4. after child exited and was reaped by wait()]
   total_pages=57066 free_pages=56685 user_pages=108 resident=108
   pt_pages=66 (user_pt=1 kernel_pt=64, +1 page directory)
   -> free pages restored: before fork=56685 after wait=56685 : NO LEAK (PASS)
[5. after 20 more fork()/wait() cycles]
   total_pages=57066 free_pages=56685 user_pages=108 resident=108
   pt_pages=66 (user_pt=1 kernel_pt=64, +1 page directory)
   -> NO LEAK after 20 cycles (PASS)
